  "result": "Perfect! All 152 tests pass. I've successfully added voucher support:\n\n**Features added:**\n\n1. **applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })** - apply discount voucher\n   - Takes fixed amount in cents off invoice (applied after VAT)\n   - Sets `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n   - Draft invoices only (returns `NOT_DRAFT` if issued/paid)\n   - One voucher per invoice (returns `VOUCHER_EXISTS` if already applied)\n   - Amount must be positive integer (returns `AMOUNT_INVALID` otherwise)\n   - Never mutates input invoice\n\n2. **invoiceTotals** - now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`\n   - `voucher`: 0 if no voucher applied, otherwise voucher amount\n   - `total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n   - Total clamped at 0 (never negative)\n   - Voucher applied AFTER VAT (not before)\n\n3. **Calculation Order**\n   - Start: subtotal (qty \u00d7 unitPrice per line)\n   - Apply: line discounts (per-line discount %)\n   - Add: VAT (on amount after discount)\n   - Apply: voucher (fixed amount off)\n   - Result: total (clamped at 0)\n\n**Test coverage (10 new voucher tests):**\n- Draft-only requirement\n- Code and amount storage\n- Duplicate voucher rejection\n- Amount validation (0, negative, decimal, non-number)\n- Input immutability\n- Voucher amount included in totals\n- Total calculation with discount + VAT + voucher\n- Total clamped at 0 with large voucher\n- Zero voucher returned when none applied\n- Correct formula: `total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n\nVouchers integrate seamlessly with existing discount and VAT system, applied last in the calculation chain.",
